Q: Why does my mouse cursor disappear in the VS Code terminal and edit windows? A: <p>Posting my solution, even though this post is quite old, because it's been bugging me for quite a while and now I finally resolved it:<br />
None of the above options worked for me, because it turned out the cursor has the same colour as the terminal background.<br />
To change it, go to <code>Code &gt; User &gt; settings.json &gt; &quot;workbench.colorCustomizations&quot;</code>  there you add</p>
<pre><code>&quot;workbench.colorCustomizations&quot;: {
  &quot;terminalCursor.foreground&quot;: &quot;#&lt;your_colour&gt;&quot;,
},
</code></pre>
<p>If you want a different colour per theme, you can do:</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>&quot;workbench.colorCustomizations&quot;: {
    &quot;[&lt;Name of dark theme&gt;]&quot;: {
      &quot;terminalCursor.foreground&quot;: &quot;#ffffff&quot;,
    },
    &quot;[&lt;Name of light theme&gt;]&quot;: {
      &quot;terminalCursor.foreground&quot;: &quot;#000000&quot;,
    },
},
</code></pre>
<p>Then restart vscode.</p>

Q: Using HTML and CSS to build a resume website. Can&#39;t get div element within body to span height of site A: <p>The issue is that <code>.left</code> has <code>position: absolute</code>, so <code>height: 100%</code> depends on its positioned parent, and your <code>html/body</code> setup doesn't guarantee the height you expect.</p>
<p>If you want the sidebar to cover the full viewport, try:</p>
<pre class="lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.left {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 25%;
    background-color: #191f41;
}
</code></pre>
<p>You can also use <code>min-height: 100vh</code> instead of <code>height: 100%</code>. If the sidebar should grow with the page content rather than the viewport, you'll need a different layout approach, such as Flexbox or Grid.</p>
